is missing the `DiagnosticsStore`.\r\n- Clear the buffer if `DiagnosticsStore` is missing to prevent growing the buffer.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n- None.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/21550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/21550/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":20468200808,"node_id":"REFE_lADODf6-U87Rjgk9zwAAAATD__Vo","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/events/20468200808","actor":{"login":"github-merge-queue[bot]","id":118344674,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBw3L4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-merge-queue%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-merge-queue","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-merge-queue%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-merge-queue%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-merge-queue%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-merge-queue%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-merge-queue%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-merge-queue%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-merge-queue%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-merge-queue%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-merge-queue%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"referenced","commit_id":"8253eabe593ce35845212dad9a3281e6b37fe18b","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/commits/8253eabe593ce35845212dad9a3281e6b37fe18b","created_at":"2025-10-23T23:03:28Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/3443868327","html_url":"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/21549#issuecomment-3443868327","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/21549","id":3443868327,"node_id":"IC_kwDODf6-U87NRUKn","user":{"login":"chescock","id":8494645,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0OTQ2NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8494645?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock","html_url":"https://github.com/chescock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-24T15:55:28Z","updated_at":"2025-10-24T15:55:28Z","body":"I poked at this a bit, and after thinking through some edge cases, I think making the parameters resilient as you did in #21550 might be the correct fix here after all.  \n\nWe should make a similar change to `GizmoBuffer`.  \n\n---\n\nThe main trouble is that other code might manipulate the world between the decision to skip and the call to `apply_deferred`.  For an extreme case, consider\n\n```rust\nfn system(mut commands: Commands, mut diagnostics: If<Diagnostics>) {\n    commands.remove_resource::<DiagnosticsStore>();\n}\n```\n\nThe system will pass validation and run, but when we go to apply commands, the `apply_deferred` will first run the command to remove the resource!  \n\nSo I think `SystemBuffer` impls will need checks like you added in #21550 no matter what.  \n\n---\n\nBut there are also other edge cases where it's not clear how to decide when to skip `apply_deferred`, such as\n\n```rust\nfn system(mut diagnostics: Option<Diagnostics>) { ... }\n```\n\nwhich will run with `None` even if the resource doesn't exist, and\n\n```rust\nfn first(mut commands: Commands) -> usize { ... }\nfn second(input: In<usize>, mut diagnostics: If<Diagnostics>) { ... }\napp.add_systems(Update, first.pipe(second));\n```\n\nwhere we probably want to run commands from `first` even if `second` skips.  \n\nI don't see any clear place to handle those cases outside of the `SystemBuffer` impl itself.  ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bevyengine/bevy/issues/comments/3443868327/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"chescock","id":8494645,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0OTQ2NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8494645?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock","html_url":"https://github.com/chescock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chescock/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}}]